  "narrative": "The new validation for H100 is consistent in point estimate but too imprecise to confirm the PTEN-loss subgroup effect. Discovery showed CDKN2A-loss lines, compared with CDKN2A-intact lines, having stronger dependency_MDM2 within PTEN-loss cells: signed effect +0.125 [0.029, 0.221], close to but just above the approximate MDM2 clinical benchmark near 0.027. Independent validation gave +0.111 [-0.026, 0.248]. The validation point estimate is clinically meaningful and in the same direction, but the 99.6% interval crosses zero and its lower bound is below both null and the approximate benchmark. With only 61 validation CDKN2A-loss cells, this small co-alteration stratum remains uncertain. I therefore keep H100 unresolved and deprioritize it as deferred. This does not weaken the primary CDKN2A-loss association with dependency_MDM2, which is accepted and independently validated broadly in H82 and supported across several TP53-state and co-alteration contexts. More broadly, the supported dataset associations are: SMARCA4 loss with much stronger dependency_SMARCA2, including MTAP-loss contexts; TP53 wild-type versus TP53 loss with much stronger dependency_USP7, including CDKN2A-loss and MTAP-loss contexts; KEAP1 loss with weaker dependency_NFE2L2, including STK11-loss contexts; MSI-high with much stronger dependency_WRN, including Avana, adenocarcinoma, BRCA2-intact, and higher-mutation-burden contexts; PTEN loss with much stronger dependency_STAT3, including PIK3CA-wild-type, PIK3CA-mutant, KEAP1-loss, CDKN2A-loss, Avana, and adenocarcinoma contexts; and CDKN2A loss with much stronger dependency_MDM2, including TP53-wild-type, TP53-loss, MTAP-intact, marker-D-negative, Avana, and adenocarcinoma contexts. Major negative or non-supported findings include broad KRAS-mutation, BRAF-V600E, EGFR-amplification, and broad ERBB2 amplification associations with their own driver dependencies in the expected direction; MYC amplification with RPL11, POLR2A, or DHX9 dependency; broad NF1-loss with dependency_KRAS in the registered direction; KRAS mutation with stronger dependency_ERBB2; and PTEN-independent PIK3CA mutation with stronger dependency_STAT3. Unresolved but low-priority areas include the PTEN-loss CDKN2A/MDM2 co-context, remaining RTK/RAS cross-talk near-null effects, broad TP53 effects on dependency_MDM2, and several untested robustness contexts. The next most informative analyses are the existing active DNA-complete checks H86-H89, pure-driver KRAS and BRAF comparisons H28/H29, PTEN-loss STAT3 in non-Avana screens H67, and SMARCA2 co-loss contexts H55/H56, plus the newly registered pure EGFR comparison and CDKN2A-loss MDM2 comparison in non-Avana screens. These test whether accepted associations persist under genomic completeness, driver purity, library variation, and additional co-loss settings. All statements remain associations in this supplied dataset and do not establish causality or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 7 synthesize: H100 validation was direction-consistent but imprecise: discovery +0.125 [0.029,0.221], validation +0.111 [-0.026,0.248]. Because validation does not confirm the small PTEN-loss subgroup, H100 remains unresolved and is deferred. Primary CDKN2A/MDM2 association remains accepted and validated (H82). Deferred low-priority broad TP53/MDM2 claims H5 and H40 because CDKN2A loss is the better MDM2 predictor and TP53 main effects remain imprecise/near null. Supported accepted clusters: SMARCA4->SMARCA2, TP53 wildtype->USP7, KEAP1 loss->weaker NFE2L2, MSI-high->WRN, PTEN loss->STAT3, CDKN2A loss->MDM2. Next analyze priorities: DNA-complete robustness H86-H89, pure-driver H28/H29 and new pure EGFR, PTEN/STAT3 non-Avana H67, SMARCA2 co-loss H55/H56, and new CDKN2A non-Avana. H100 is low priority unless a more powerful external co-context becomes available."
